  "description": "Ternary Bonsai 2 27B MLX inference speedup track (prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-mlx-2bit @ 3f926b415992eaa2ae9dd7b573706494d6bbf787, a 2-bit affine group-128 MLX pack of Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B with a signed block Walsh-Hadamard transform, block 1024, on the input of every packed projection). The text tower is 64 layers on a four-layer repeat: 16 full-attention layers (24 query heads over 4 KV heads at head_dim 256, at every index % 4 == 3) and 48 gated-delta-net linear-attention layers (16 key heads and 48 value heads of dim 128, conv kernel 4, FP32 state). Hidden size 5120, vocabulary 248320, untied embeddings. There are TWO speculative decoders, each a SEPARATE pinned export that shares the target's embeddings and output head: the MTP head EigenLabs/Qwen3.8-27B-MTP-4bit @ 329261c5e0b3f9c233485e682cb3b67b88c20a55 at draft depth 1 to 7, and the DFlash 2 block drafter z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 @ 50307d4c4cde6860d4eee73e2547cd786fe8e8a4 at draft depth 1 to 16. mtp-head.manifest.json is a DECLARATION only: it is editable and optional, spec.decoder names the decoder (mtp or dflash), and it accepts source 'pinned' only. Both decoders are single-stream (maximum speculative batch 1). The KV backend is pinned contiguous. The target model may never be re-quantized. Optimize the Bonsai 2 and Qwen 3.5 model files, the offline transform, and the vendored MLX/Metal kernel families the forward pass dispatches. Scoring is paired single-stream on the same box: a serial control leg on the organizer's reference tree versus the declared decoder and depth, composite = prefill_gain^0.25 * decode_gain^0.75. docs/participant-contract.md section 5 is the authority.",
